1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,050
What if the world forgot one word every day?

2
00:00:03,090 --> 00:00:04,986
Monday, nobody can say cheese.

3
00:00:05,026 --> 00:00:07,116
The sign above the shop flickers,

4
00:00:07,156 --> 00:00:10,924
the letters melt, and everyone just points at the sandwich.

5
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:13,785
Tuesday, it's the word umbrella.

6
00:00:13,825 --> 00:00:14,780
Wednesday, bicycle.

7
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:16,403
You invent clumsy replacements,

8
00:00:16,443 --> 00:00:18,183
like rain hat and two-wheel horse.

9
00:00:18,223 --> 00:00:20,435
Dictionaries shrink a little every morning,

10
00:00:20,475 --> 00:00:22,110
like autumn trees losing leaves.

11
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:25,894
By week two, people start talking in gestures.

12
00:00:25,934 --> 00:00:28,366
Waiters mime orders, teachers draw pictures,

13
00:00:28,406 --> 00:00:30,726
and street signs become tiny comic strips.

14
00:00:30,766 --> 00:00:33,310
Honestly, it's quieter, and kind of beautiful.

15
00:00:34,550 --> 00:00:35,653
By day one hundred,

16
00:00:35,693 --> 00:00:37,699
the big words start vanishing too.

17
00:00:37,739 --> 00:00:38,241
Tomorrow.

18
00:00:38,281 --> 00:00:38,602
Sorry.

19
00:00:38,642 --> 00:00:39,023
Friend.

20
00:00:39,063 --> 00:00:40,226
Nobody can say them,

21
00:00:40,266 --> 00:00:41,490
so people hold doors,

22
00:00:41,530 --> 00:00:43,897
share umbrellas, and bring soup instead.

23
00:00:43,937 --> 00:00:45,581
Actions speak louder anyway.

24
00:00:46,850 --> 00:00:48,898
Scientists would call this impossible,

25
00:00:48,938 --> 00:00:50,821
since words don't vanish overnight.

26
00:00:50,861 --> 00:00:52,305
In this thought experiment,

27
00:00:52,345 --> 00:00:54,887
though, language slowly empties like a bathtub,

28
00:00:54,927 --> 00:00:56,810
and you can almost hear the gurgle.

29
00:00:58,050 --> 00:00:59,059
Day two hundred.

30
00:00:59,099 --> 00:01:00,698
The word love disappears.

31
00:01:00,738 --> 00:01:03,713
Couples stare at each other, completely stuck.

32
00:01:03,753 --> 00:01:05,090
Then, without a word,

33
00:01:05,130 --> 00:01:06,532
he hands her an apple,

34
00:01:06,572 --> 00:01:08,367
and she hands him her scarf.

35
00:01:09,550 --> 00:01:10,604
Here's the twist.

36
00:01:10,644 --> 00:01:12,922
When the dictionary is nearly empty,

37
00:01:12,962 --> 00:01:15,046
people invent new words together.

38
00:01:15,086 --> 00:01:16,526
Gloop means happy rain.

39
00:01:16,566 --> 00:01:18,522
Fizz means a hug from far away.

40
00:01:18,562 --> 00:01:20,581
Language is never gone for long.

41
00:01:21,850 --> 00:01:24,519
So every morning, the town gathers to invent

42
00:01:24,559 --> 00:01:26,059
tomorrow's word together.

43
00:01:26,099 --> 00:01:27,844
Today's winner is a tiny kid,

44
00:01:27,884 --> 00:01:30,308
who points at the sunrise and says: wow.

45
00:01:30,348 --> 00:01:31,293
Everyone agrees.

46
00:01:31,333 --> 00:01:32,524
It means everything.
